s='''<nav><a href="/">← Aleph</a> · <a href="/gate-da-dbms/">Existing DBMS Round1 pack</a></nav><section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">GATE DA · Three-week DBMS review</p><h1>Model the data.<br>Follow the query.<br>Check the assumptions.</h1><p class="sub">Week1 contains seven review lessons with original exam-pattern practice, worked review, big-picture summaries and mind maps.</p><p>Primary reference: Database System Concepts, seventh edition, Silberschatz, Korth and Sudarshan. Targeted supplement: Data Mining: Concepts and Techniques, third edition, Han, Kamber and Pei.</p><p>The recorded plan places this review after DBMS Round1. Material is ready for that review; no completion or start date is assumed.</p></section><div class="phase-grid"><section><h2>Week1 · Review and diagnose</h2><p>Days1–7 revisit the whole database/warehousing/preprocessing scope. Each has exposition, two examples, five practice questions, worked review, a fresh check and a mind map. Available now.</p></section><section id="week2"><h2>Week2 · Mixed exam applications</h2><p>Days8–14 use official problem families with new data and mixed conditions. Adjust emphasis using Week1 responses. Daily material is planned, not authored.</p></section><section><h2>Week3 · Review and remedy</h2><p>Days15–21 target confirmed errors, then test transfer and delayed retrieval. Daily material depends on earlier evidence and is not yet authored.</p></section></div><section class="panel"><h2>The book–syllabus intersection</h2><p>The official DA2027 Section5 includes both databases and analytical data preparation. A SQL-only review would leave out explicit requirements. Selected chapters from the chosen DBMS book supply the database core; the preprocessing supplement fills the transformation scope. Schema normalization and numeric normalization remain separate topics.</p><div class="overlap"><table><thead><tr><th>Syllabus topic</th><th>Selected reading</th><th>Observed official question families</th><th>Day</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''
