s+='''</tbody></table></div><p>Transactions, locking/recovery, distributed consensus and the full query-optimizer machinery are valuable book material but are not separately named in DA2027 Section5, so they do not displace the explicit first-week topics. Higher normal-form extensions can be selected in Week2 where appropriate. No score weighting is inferred from this small set of papers.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Seven days of material</h2><ol class="toc">'''
for d in D:s+=f'<li><a href="day-{d["day"]:02}.html">Day{d["day"]} · {E(d["title"])}</a><p>{E(d["goal"])}</p></li>'
s+='''</ol><p>Every day has two multi-select questions and three short computations/explanations, ten learning-diagnostic points. The examples are original; the linked official papers establish problem families, not copied prompts or answers. Questions are designed to expose the first mistaken assumption, not just a wrong final number.</p><p>Record the original attempt before opening worked review. The reading-page record is browser-local and exportable. For a server submission and the existing AI feedback workflow, upload under <strong>Aleph → Subjects → DBMS: three-week review</strong>. The original DBMS pack and its flashcard/review workflow remain available.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>The next fourteen study days</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Day</th><th>Planned review focus</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''
plan=[(8,'Integrity/ER design with relational query consequences'),(9,'Relational algebra, division and quantified calculus'),(10,'SQL bag/NULL/group/correlation mixtures'),(11,'Closure, keys, decomposition and selected higher normal forms'),(12,'File layout, B+ updates and access-path cost mixtures'),(13,'Cube/hierarchy/measure questions and preprocessing transfer'),(14,'Mixed timed review across all seven topics'),(15,'Reconstruct the largest confirmed Week2 errors'),(16,'Repair representation, quantifier and null-semantics gaps'),(17,'Repair dependency/decomposition reasoning'),(18,'Repair page-layout and aggregation computations'),(19,'New-surface transfer without prior solution prompts'),(20,'Delayed mixed reattempt and explain-back'),(21,'Final diagnostic, concept-map reconstruction and next steps')]
for day,title in plan:s+=f'<tr><td>{day}</td><td>{E(title)}</td></tr>'
s+='''</tbody></table><p>Relative study days only. Weeks2–3 are outlines; their actual repair mix must follow the submitted work. No DBMS Round1 completion, mastery, study time or calendar commitment is inferred.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>The big picture</h2><svg class="mindmap" viewBox="0 0 1000 440" role="img" aria-label="DBMS review concept map"><title>Database models, queries, storage and analytics</title><rect x="15" y="175" width="235" height="85" rx="12" fill="#176955"/><text x="132" y="223" fill="white" text-anchor="middle" font-size="24">DBMS review</text><g fill="none" stroke="#7d9eae" stroke-width="2"><path d="M250 217 C320 217 330 57 385 57"/><path d="M250 217 C320 217 330 163 385 163"/><path d="M250 217 C320 217 330 269 385 269"/><path d="M250 217 C320 217 330 375 385 375"/></g><g fill="#eef4f7" stroke="#a4bac4"><rect x="385" y="12" width="600" height="92" rx="8"/><rect x="385" y="118" width="600" height="92" rx="8"/><rect x="385" y="224" width="600" height="92" rx="8"/><rect x="385" y="330" width="600" height="92" rx="8"/></g><g fill="#19343c" font-family="system-ui" font-size="21"><text x="405" y="43">Model legal information</text><text x="405" y="78">Entities, keys, constraints and dependencies</text><text x="405" y="149">Ask precise questions</text><text x="405" y="184">Algebra/calculus sets; SQL bags and nulls</text><text x="405" y="255">Choose physical access</text><text x="405" y="290">Record/page layout; indexes; query predicates</text><text x="405" y="361">Prepare and summarize</text><text x="405" y="396">Warehouse grain, measures and transformations</text></g></svg><p>A logical schema defines permitted information. A query defines a result under specific semantics. Storage determines access cost. Analytical summaries and transformations must preserve the information needed for their purpose.</p></section><section class="panel" id="sources"><h2>Verified references and paper evidence</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.db-book.com/">Database System Concepts7e, authors’ site</a>; <a href="https://www.db-book.com/toc-dir/toc.pdf">official contents</a>; <a href="https://www.db-book.com/online-chapters-dir/27.pdf">Chapter27, formal relational languages</a>.</li><li><a href="https://hanj.cs.illinois.edu/bk3/bk3_slidesindex.htm">Han, Kamber and Pei3e, authors’ chapter resources</a>: Chapter3 preprocessing and selected Chapters4–5 warehousing/cube material. These are limited supplements, not an additional whole-book assignment.</li><li><a href="https://gate2027.iitm.ac.in/static/doc/GATE2027_Syllabus/DA_GATE2027_Syllabus.pdf">Official GATE DA2027 syllabus</a>, Section5, checked November8,2026.</li><li><a href="https://gate2026.iitg.ac.in/doc/download/2024/DA24S1.pdf">Official DA2024 paper</a>; <a href="https://gate2026.iitg.ac.in/doc/download/2025/DA2025.pdf">DA2025 paper</a>; <a href="https://gate2026.iitg.ac.in/doc/download/2026/QPs/DA.pdf">DA2026 paper</a>. Daily links identify question numbers/pages. <a href="evidence.json">Pattern/source ledger</a>.</li></ul><p>We inspected the selected official question families and the existing DBMS pack’s source ledger. No claim is made to have newly graded every historical question. In particular, an existing caveat on the accepted range for DA2026 Q59 is not transferred to the new unambiguous practice. Sampling/compression coverage follows the explicit syllabus; it is not represented as an observed question family in the selected papers.</p></section>'''
